IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 5 Division 3, ss 184, 185, 186, 187 -- special resolutions, special notice, lodging copies, adjourned meetings.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Percentages and fractions are tested by integer comparison, never by division.
-- Written resolutions (ss 184A to 184G) are a separate module.
-- "Days' notice": the number of days is an input the person counts; the text does not say "clear days" and the keel assumes no ruling (marginal reading in NOTES.md).

§ `Section 184(1) and (2): when a resolution is a special resolution`

-- (1): "A resolution is a special resolution when it has been passed by a majority of not less than three-fourths of such members as, being entitled to do so, vote in person or, where proxies are allowed, by proxy present
-- at a general meeting of which -- (a) in the case of a private company -- not less than 14 days' written notice; or (b) in the case of a public company -- not less than 21 days' written notice, specifying the intention
-- to propose the resolution as a special resolution has been duly given."
-- src:16551 | 184.—(1) A resolution is a special resolution when it has been
-- src:16552 | passed by a majority of not less than three‑fourths of such members
-- src:16557 | as, being entitled to do so, vote in person or, where proxies are
-- src:16558 | allowed, by proxy present at a general meeting of which —
-- src:16560 | (a) in the case of a private company — not less than 14 days’
-- src:16561 | written notice; or
-- src:16563 | (b) in the case of a public company — not less than 21 days’
-- src:16564 | written notice,
-- src:16566 | specifying the intention to propose the resolution as a special
-- src:16567 | resolution has been duly given.
@ref s 184(1) (src:16551-16567)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 184(1) the number of days' written notice the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the company is a private company` THEN 14 ELSE 21

-- The majority: "a majority of not less than three-fourths of such members as, being entitled to do so, vote". 4 times those in favour is at least 3 times all who vote; nobody voting is no majority.
@ref s 184(1) (src:16551-16567)
GIVEN `the number voting in favour` IS A NUMBER
      `the number voting against` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 184(1) the number voting in favour is not less than three-fourths of those voting` MEANS
        `the number voting in favour` PLUS `the number voting against` GREATER THAN 0
    AND 4 TIMES `the number voting in favour` AT LEAST 3 TIMES (`the number voting in favour` PLUS `the number voting against`)

@ref s 184(1) (src:16551-16567)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number voting in favour` IS A NUMBER
      `the number voting against` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days of written notice given of the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice specified the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(1) the resolution is a special resolution` MEANS
    IF    `s 184(1) the number voting in favour is not less than three-fourths of those voting` `the number voting in favour` `the number voting against`
      AND `the notice specified the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution`
      AND (`the number of days of written notice given of the meeting` AT LEAST `s 184(1) the number of days' written notice the subsection requires` `the company is a private company` OR `the answer under subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A resolution is a special resolution when it has been passed by a majority of not less than three-fourths ... at a general meeting of which ... not less than 14 days' written notice ...; or ... 21 days' written notice, specifying the intention to propose the resolution as a special resolution has been duly given" (a "means"-style definition; a limb unmet; subsection (2)'s shorter notice counted when it is met)

-- (2): "Despite subsection (1), if it so agreed by a majority in number of the members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting, being a majority which together holds not less than 95% of the total voting rights
-- of all the members having a right to vote at that meeting, a resolution may be proposed and passed as a special resolution at a meeting of which written notice of a period less than that required under subsection (1)
-- has been given." A power gated "if": NOTHING when the gate fails (grant ruling, limit 1; F-41).
-- src:16569 | (2) Despite subsection (1), if it so agreed by a majority in number of
-- src:16570 | the members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting, being
-- src:16571 | a majority which together holds not less than 95% of the total voting
-- src:16572 | rights of all the members having a right to vote at that meeting, a
-- src:16573 | resolution may be proposed and passed as a special resolution at a
-- src:16574 | meeting of which written notice of a period less than that required
-- src:16575 | under subsection (1) has been given.
@ref s 184(2) (src:16569-16575)
GIVEN `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting who agreed to the shorter notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the voting rights held by the members who agreed` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(2) the resolution may be proposed and passed as a special resolution on shorter notice` MEANS
    IF    `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting` GREATER THAN 0
      AND 2 TIMES `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting who agreed to the shorter notice` GREATER THAN `the number of members having the right to attend and vote at the meeting`
      AND `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting` GREATER THAN 0
      AND 100 TIMES `the voting rights held by the members who agreed` AT LEAST 95 TIMES `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it so agreed by a majority in number of the members ..., being a majority which together holds not less than 95% of the total voting rights ..., a resolution may be proposed and passed as a special resolution" (a grant whose "if" gate failed; F-41)

§ `Section 184(3) to (6): the chairperson's declaration, a poll, and deemed notice`

-- src:16577 | (3) At any meeting at which a special resolution is submitted, a
-- src:16578 | declaration of the chairperson that the resolution is carried is unless a
-- src:16579 | poll is demanded conclusive evidence of the fact without proof of the
-- src:16580 | number or proportion of the votes recorded in favour of or against the
-- src:16581 | resolution.
@ref s 184(3) (src:16577-16581)
GIVEN `the chairperson has declared that the resolution is carried` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a poll is demanded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(3) the chairperson's declaration is conclusive evidence that the resolution is carried` MEANS
    IF NOT `the chairperson has declared that the resolution is carried`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "a declaration of the chairperson that the resolution is carried"
    ELSE (IF `a poll is demanded`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a declaration of the chairperson that the resolution is carried is unless a poll is demanded conclusive evidence" -- a poll is demanded, so this subsection gives no conclusive evidence on these facts (an "unless" once met; decided case by case, F-42)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (4): "a poll is deemed to be effectively demanded if demanded -- (a) by such number of members for the time being entitled under the constitution to vote at the meeting as is specified in the constitution, but it is not in any
-- case necessary for more than 5 members to make the demand; (b) if no such provision is made by the constitution -- by 3 members so entitled, or by one or 2 members so entitled, if -- (i) that member holds or those 2 members
-- together hold not less than 10% of the total number of paid-up shares of the company (excluding treasury shares); or (ii) that member represents or those 2 members together represent not less than 10% of the total voting rights".
-- (4A): "any reference to a member does not include a reference to a company itself where it is registered as a member": such a member is taken off the count of members demanding.
-- src:16583 | (4) At any meeting at which a special resolution is submitted, a poll
-- src:16584 | is deemed to be effectively demanded if demanded —
-- src:16586 | (a) by such number of members for the time being entitled
-- src:16587 | under the constitution to vote at the meeting as is specified
-- src:16588 | in the constitution, but it is not in any case necessary for
-- src:16589 | more than 5 members to make the demand;
-- src:16591 | (b) if no such provision is made by the constitution — by
-- src:16592 | 3 members so entitled, or by one or 2 members so entitled,
-- src:16593 | if —
-- src:16595 | (i) that member holds or those 2 members together hold
-- src:16596 | not less than 10% of the total number of paid‑up
-- src:16597 | shares of the company (excluding treasury shares);
-- src:16598 | or
-- src:16603 | (ii) that member represents or those 2 members together
-- src:16604 | represent not less than 10% of the total voting rights
-- src:16605 | of all the members having a right to vote at that
-- src:16606 | meeting.
@ref s 184(4) (src:16583-16606)
GIVEN `the number of members entitled to vote who demand a poll` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of them that are the company itself registered as a member` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members the constitution specifies for a demand` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the number of paid-up shares the members demanding hold` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of paid-up shares of the company excluding treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the voting rights the members demanding represent` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(4) a poll is deemed to be effectively demanded` MEANS
    LET demanding MEANS `the number of members entitled to vote who demand a poll` MINUS `the number of them that are the company itself registered as a member`
    IN CONSIDER `the number of members the constitution specifies for a demand`
       WHEN JUST specified THEN
           (IF demanding AT LEAST (IF specified GREATER THAN 5 THEN 5 ELSE specified)
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a poll is deemed to be effectively demanded if demanded -- (a) by such number of members ... as is specified in the constitution, but it is not in any case necessary for more than 5 members to make the demand" (an "if" gate on a deeming read as no when failed, marginal reading (a); F-15)
       WHEN NOTHING THEN
           (IF    demanding AT LEAST 3
               OR (    demanding AT LEAST 1 AND demanding AT MOST 2
                   AND (   (`the total number of paid-up shares of the company excluding treasury shares` GREATER THAN 0 AND 100 TIMES `the number of paid-up shares the members demanding hold` AT LEAST 10 TIMES `the total number of paid-up shares of the company excluding treasury shares`)
                        OR (`the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting` GREATER THAN 0 AND 100 TIMES `the voting rights the members demanding represent` AT LEAST 10 TIMES `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting`)))
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if no such provision is made by the constitution -- by 3 members so entitled, or by one or 2 members so entitled, if -- (i) ... not less than 10% of the total number of paid-up shares ...; or (ii) ... not less than 10% of the total voting rights" (an "if" gate on a deeming read as no when failed, marginal reading (a); F-15)

-- src:16610 | (4A) For the purposes of subsection (4), any reference to a member
-- src:16611 | does not include a reference to a company itself where it is registered
-- src:16612 | as a member.
@ref s 184(4A) (src:16610-16612)
GIVEN `the registered member is the company itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(4A) the registered member is a member for the purposes of subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the registered member is the company itself`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any reference to a member does not include a reference to a company itself where it is registered as a member" (a flat negative; N2)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of the company itself as a registered member

-- src:16614 | (5) In computing the majority on a poll demanded on the question
-- src:16615 | that a special resolution be passed, reference must be had to the
-- src:16616 | number of votes cast for and against the resolution and to the number
-- src:16617 | of votes to which each member is entitled by this Act or the
-- src:16618 | constitution of the company.
@ref s 184(5) (src:16614-16618)
GIVEN `the number of votes cast for the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of votes cast against the resolution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 184(5) the majority on the poll is not less than three-fourths` MEANS
    `s 184(1) the number voting in favour is not less than three-fourths of those voting` `the number of votes cast for the resolution` `the number of votes cast against the resolution`

-- src:16622 | (6) For the purposes of this section, notice of a meeting is deemed to
-- src:16623 | be duly given and the meeting is deemed to be duly held when the
-- src:16624 | notice is given and the meeting held in the manner provided by this
-- src:16625 | Act or by the constitution.
@ref s 184(6) (src:16622-16625)
GIVEN `the notice is given in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(6) notice of the meeting is deemed to be duly given` MEANS
    IF `the notice is given in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "notice of a meeting is deemed to be duly given ... when the notice is given ... in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution" (a "when" gate on a deeming, counted as "where"; periods ruling (b))

@ref s 184(6) (src:16622-16625)
GIVEN `the notice is given in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is held in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(6) the meeting is deemed to be duly held` MEANS
    IF `the notice is given in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution` AND `the meeting is held in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the meeting is deemed to be duly held when the notice is given and the meeting held in the manner provided by this Act or by the constitution" (a "when" gate on a deeming, counted as "where"; periods ruling (b))

§ `Section 184(7) and (8): extraordinary resolutions`

-- src:16629 | (7) Any extraordinary resolution, duly and appropriately passed
-- src:16630 | before 29 December 1967 is for the purposes of this Act treated as a
-- src:16631 | special resolution.
@ref s 184(7) (src:16629-16631)
GIVEN `the date the extraordinary resolution was passed` IS A DATE
      `it was duly and appropriately passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(7) the extraordinary resolution is treated as a special resolution for the purposes of this Act` MEANS
    IF `the date the extraordinary resolution was passed` LESS THAN `the day 29 December 1967` AND `it was duly and appropriately passed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any extraordinary resolution, duly and appropriately passed before 29 December 1967 is for the purposes of this Act treated as a special resolution" (a scope limit with no "only"; periods ruling (c))

-- src:16633 | (8) Where in the case of a company incorporated before
-- src:16634 | 29 December 1967 any matter is required or permitted to be done
-- src:16635 | by extraordinary resolution, that matter may be done by special
-- src:16636 | resolution.
@ref s 184(8) (src:16633-16636)
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `a matter is required or permitted to be done by extraordinary resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 184(8) the matter may be done by special resolution` MEANS
    IF `the date the company was incorporated` LESS THAN `the day 29 December 1967` AND `a matter is required or permitted to be done by extraordinary resolution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in the case of a company incorporated before 29 December 1967 any matter is required or permitted to be done by extraordinary resolution, that matter may be done by special resolution" (a "where" gate on a "may": periods ruling (b); split site (ii), F-43)

§ `Section 185: special notice`

-- 185 (first limb): "Where by this Act special notice is required of a resolution, the resolution is not effective unless notice of the intention to move it has been given to the company not less than 28 days before the meeting at which it is moved".
-- "but if after notice of the intention to move such a resolution has been given to the company, a meeting is called for a date 28 days or less after the notice has been given, the notice, although not given to the company
-- within the time required by this section, is deemed to be properly given." The answer is the bar: JUST TRUE means the resolution is not effective for want of the notice.
-- src:16932 | 185. Where by this Act special notice is required of a resolution, the
-- src:16933 | resolution is not effective unless notice of the intention to move it has
-- src:16934 | been given to the company not less than 28 days before the meeting at
-- src:16935 | which it is moved, and the company must give its members notice of
-- src:16936 | any such resolution at the same time and in the same manner as it
-- src:16937 | gives notice of the meeting or, if that is not practicable, must give
-- src:16938 | them notice thereof, in any manner allowed by the constitution, not
-- src:16939 | less than 14 days before the meeting, but if after notice of the
-- src:16940 | intention to move such a resolution has been given to the company, a
-- src:16941 | meeting is called for a date 28 days or less after the notice has been
-- src:16942 | given, the notice, although not given to the company within the time
-- src:16943 | required by this section, is deemed to be properly given.
@ref s 185 (src:16932-16943)
GIVEN `special notice is required of the resolution by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day notice of the intention to move the resolution was given to the company` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting at which it is moved` IS A DATE
      `a meeting was called after that notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185 the resolution is not effective because notice of the intention to move it was not given to the company in time` MEANS
    IF NOT `special notice is required of the resolution by this Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where by this Act special notice is required of a resolution, the resolution is not effective unless ..." (a "where" gate on a bar: the bar does not apply)
    ELSE (IF    `period: the date is at least a period before` `the day notice of the intention to move the resolution was given to the company` `the day of the meeting at which it is moved` 28 Days
             OR (`a meeting was called after that notice was given` AND `the day of the meeting at which it is moved` AT MOST `period: the last day of a period after` `the day notice of the intention to move the resolution was given to the company` 28 Days)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): notice given not less than 28 days before the meeting, or deemed properly given ("a meeting is called for a date 28 days or less after the notice has been given"): the "unless" is met
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- the company's duty to its members: "the company must give its members notice of any such resolution at the same time and in the same manner as it gives notice of the meeting or, if that is not practicable, must give them
-- notice thereof, in any manner allowed by the constitution, not less than 14 days before the meeting".
@ref s 185 (src:16932-16943)
GIVEN `special notice is required of the resolution by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company gave members notice at the same time and in the same manner as notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was not practicable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company gave members notice in a manner allowed by the constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company gave members notice` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting at which it is moved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 185 the company has given its members notice of the resolution as the section requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `special notice is required of the resolution by this Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where by this Act special notice is required of a resolution, ... the company must give its members notice" (a "where" gate on a duty)
    ELSE (IF    `the company gave members notice at the same time and in the same manner as notice of the meeting`
             OR (    `it was not practicable to do so` AND `the company gave members notice in a manner allowed by the constitution`
                 AND `period: the date is at least a period before` `the day the company gave members notice` `the day of the meeting at which it is moved` 14 Days)
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must give its members notice of any such resolution at the same time and in the same manner as it gives notice of the meeting or, if that is not practicable, must give them notice thereof, in any manner allowed by the constitution, not less than 14 days before the meeting" (a duty's own question)

§ `Section 186: lodging copies of resolutions`

-- (1): "A copy of -- (a) every special resolution; and (b) every resolution, including any resolution passed under section 175A(1)(a), which effectively binds any class of shareholders whether agreed to by all the members of that
-- class or not, must, except where otherwise expressly provided by this Act within 14 days after the passing or making thereof, be lodged by the company with the Registrar."
-- src:16952 | 186.—(1) A copy of —
-- src:16954 | (a) every special resolution; and
-- src:16956 | (b) every resolution, including any resolution passed under
-- src:16957 | section 175A(1)(a), which effectively binds any class of
-- src:16958 | shareholders whether agreed to by all the members of that
-- src:16959 | class or not,
-- src:16961 | must, except where otherwise expressly provided by this Act within
-- src:16962 | 14 days after the passing or making thereof, be lodged by the
-- src:16963 | company with the Registrar.
@ref s 186(1) (src:16952-16963)
GIVEN `the resolution is a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution effectively binds a class of shareholders, whether agreed to by all the members of that class or not` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this Act expressly provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(1) a copy of the resolution must be lodged by the company with the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `this Act expressly provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "except where otherwise expressly provided by this Act" -- the other provision governs
    ELSE (IF `the resolution is a special resolution` OR `the resolution effectively binds a class of shareholders, whether agreed to by all the members of that class or not`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A copy of -- (a) every special resolution; and (b) every resolution ... which effectively binds any class of shareholders ... must ... be lodged" (a duty's own question; neither limb)

@ref s 186(1) (src:16952-16963)
GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed or made` IS A DATE
      `the day a copy was lodged with the Registrar` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 186(1) the copy was lodged within 14 days after the passing or making` MEANS
    `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed or made` `the day a copy was lodged with the Registrar` 14 Days

GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed or made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 186(1) the number of days from the passing or making to the last day for lodging` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed or made` 14 Days) MINUS `the day the resolution was passed or made`

-- (2): "Where the constitution of a company has not been registered, a copy of every resolution to which this section applies must be forwarded to any member at the member's request on payment of $1 or such less sum as the
-- company directs." The sum due is $1, or the lesser sum the company directs.
-- src:16967 | (2) Where the constitution of a company has not been registered, a
-- src:16968 | copy of every resolution to which this section applies must be
-- src:16969 | forwarded to any member at the member’s request on payment of $1
-- src:16970 | or such less sum as the company directs.
@ref s 186(2) (src:16967-16970)
GIVEN `the sum the company directs, if it directs a sum less than $1` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 186(2) the sum the member must pay for a copy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the sum the company directs, if it directs a sum less than $1`
    WHEN JUST directed THEN (IF directed LESS THAN 1 THEN directed ELSE 1)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 1

@ref s 186(2) (src:16967-16970)
GIVEN `the constitution of the company has not been registered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is one to which section 186 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a member has requested a copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum the member has paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum the company directs, if it directs a sum less than $1` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(2) the company must forward a copy of the resolution to the member` MEANS
    IF `the constitution of the company has not been registered` AND `the resolution is one to which section 186 applies` AND `a member has requested a copy`
         AND `the sum the member has paid` AT LEAST `s 186(2) the sum the member must pay for a copy` `the sum the company directs, if it directs a sum less than $1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the constitution of a company has not been registered, a copy of every resolution to which this section applies must be forwarded to any member at the member's request on payment of $1 or such less sum as the company directs" (a "where" gate on a duty; the duty arises on request and payment)

-- src:16976 | (3) In the event of any default in complying with subsection (1) the
-- src:16977 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:16978 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:16979 | exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 186(3) (src:16976-16979)
GIVEN `there is a default in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `there is a default in complying with subsection (1)` AND `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), F-10): "In the event of any default in complying with subsection (1) the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

@ref s 186(3) (src:16976-16979)
GIVEN `there is a default in complying with subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 186(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 186(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `there is a default in complying with subsection (1)` `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $1,000, and also a default penalty; no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- src:16981 | (4) In the event of any default in complying with subsection (2), the
-- src:16982 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:16983 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine of $50
-- src:16984 | for each copy in respect of which default is made.
@ref s 186(4) (src:16981-16984)
GIVEN `there is a default in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 186(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `there is a default in complying with subsection (2)` AND `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), F-10): "In the event of any default in complying with subsection (2), the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

-- "a fine of $50 for each copy in respect of which default is made": the figure is fifty dollars times the number of copies not furnished.
@ref s 186(4) (src:16981-16984)
GIVEN `there is a default in complying with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of copies in respect of which default is made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 186(4) the fine on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 186(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `there is a default in complying with subsection (2)` `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF (50 TIMES `the number of copies in respect of which default is made`), 0, FALSE, FALSE)   -- a fine of $50 for each copy; no imprisonment; no default penalty stated
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 187: resolutions at adjourned meetings`

-- src:16988 | 187. Where a resolution is passed at an adjourned meeting of a
-- src:16989 | company or of holders of any class of shares or of directors the
-- src:16990 | resolution is for all purposes treated as having been passed on the date
-- src:16991 | on which it was in fact passed and not on any earlier date.
@ref s 187 (src:16988-16991)
GIVEN `the resolution is passed at an adjourned meeting of a company, or of holders of any class of shares, or of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which it was in fact passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 187 the date the resolution is treated as having been passed` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is passed at an adjourned meeting of a company, or of holders of any class of shares, or of directors`
    THEN JUST `the date on which it was in fact passed`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section speaks only of "a resolution ... passed at an adjourned meeting"

§ `Regulative rules of ss 185 and 186`

DECLARE `s 185 and s 186 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 185 give members notice of the resolution`
    `s 186(1) lodge a copy of the resolution with the Registrar`

-- s 185: where giving notice at the time of the notice of the meeting is not practicable, the company must give members notice not less than 14 days before the meeting. Time 0 is a stated day; the last day is 14 days before the meeting.
-- src:16932 | 185. Where by this Act special notice is required of a resolution, the
-- src:16933 | resolution is not effective unless notice of the intention to move it has
-- src:16934 | been given to the company not less than 28 days before the meeting at
-- src:16935 | which it is moved, and the company must give its members notice of
-- src:16936 | any such resolution at the same time and in the same manner as it
-- src:16937 | gives notice of the meeting or, if that is not practicable, must give
-- src:16938 | them notice thereof, in any manner allowed by the constitution, not
-- src:16939 | less than 14 days before the meeting, but if after notice of the
-- src:16940 | intention to move such a resolution has been given to the company, a
-- src:16941 | meeting is called for a date 28 days or less after the notice has been
-- src:16942 | given, the notice, although not given to the company within the time
-- src:16943 | required by this section, is deemed to be properly given.
@ref s 185 (src:16932-16943)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the day taken as time 0` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting at which the resolution is moved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 185 and s 186 act`
`s 185 the company must give its members notice of the resolution not less than 14 days before the meeting where giving it with the notice of the meeting is not practicable` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 185 give members notice of the resolution`
    WITHIN ((`period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the day of the meeting at which the resolution is moved` 14 Days) MINUS `the day taken as time 0`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not give its members notice of the resolution not less than 14 days before the meeting"

-- s 186(1): time 0 is the day the resolution is passed or made; the last day is 14 days later.
-- src:16952 | 186.—(1) A copy of —
-- src:16954 | (a) every special resolution; and
-- src:16956 | (b) every resolution, including any resolution passed under
-- src:16957 | section 175A(1)(a), which effectively binds any class of
-- src:16958 | shareholders whether agreed to by all the members of that
-- src:16959 | class or not,
-- src:16961 | must, except where otherwise expressly provided by this Act within
-- src:16962 | 14 days after the passing or making thereof, be lodged by the
-- src:16963 | company with the Registrar.
@ref s 186(1) (src:16952-16963)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 185 and s 186 act`
`s 186(1) the company must lodge a copy of the resolution with the Registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 186(1) lodge a copy of the resolution with the Registrar`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not lodge a copy of the resolution with the Registrar within 14 days after the passing or making of the resolution"
